# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Next.js App Router + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Vitest.
Architecture and future feature instructions are in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md).

```bash
npm run dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000`. The starter uses system fonts, so production builds
do not download a font. Use a Node release supported by the installed packages
(a current Node 24 LTS release is a suitable starting point). `.node-version`
records the runtime used at initialization. Commit
`package-lock.json` and use `npm ci` for subsequent installs.

```text
src/app/                       Next.js routing and runtime adapters
src/features/<feature>/
  domain/                      business entities and rules
  application/                 use cases and consumed ports
  infrastructure/              network/storage implementations and mapping
  presentation/                React UI, hooks, and view state
src/composition/               separate server/client dependency wiring
src/shared/ui/                 shared presentation primitives
```

Request `add-nextjs-feature <feature description>`, or describe a frontend feature
normally in this project. The saved instructions apply without repeating the
architecture requirement. Replace the `home` starter as the product takes shape;
inner directories are populated only when business behavior needs them.

Checks:

```bash
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run build
```

`npm run test:watch` starts Vitest in watch mode. `*.test.ts` uses Node;
`*.test.tsx` uses jsdom and React Testing Library. For async Server Components
or runtime routing/authentication, add the relevant integration/E2E coverage;
the starter component test does not exercise those Next.js runtime features.

Production preview: `npm run build` followed by `npm start`.
